        <h1>Privacy Policy for DailyMate</h1>
        <p class="date">Effective Date: October 20, 2026</p>

        <p>DailyMate ("we", "our", or "us") operates the DailyMate mobile application (the "App"). This page informs you of our policies regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal data when you use our App and the choices you have associated with that data.</p>

        <h2>1. Information Collection and Use</h2>
        <p>We collect several different types of information for various purposes to provide and improve our App to you.</p>
        
        <h3>Types of Data Collected:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Personal Data:</strong> When you sign in using Google Authentication or create an account, we may collect your name, email address, and profile picture to sync your habits, tasks, and notes securely.</li>
            <li><strong>Usage Data & Habit Records:</strong> We store your habits, daily streaks, completion history, task lists, and notes either locally on your device or in secure cloud databases (Firebase Firestore) if cloud sync is enabled.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Advertising and Google AdMob</h2>
        <p>To support the development and maintenance of DailyMate, we may integrate <strong>Google AdMob</strong> in future updates to display advertisements. Google AdMob may use device identifiers, advertising IDs, and cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to our app or other apps on the internet.</p>
        <p>You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting Google's Ads Settings. AdMob's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to our users based on their visit to your apps and/or other apps on the Internet.</p>

        <h2>3. Use of Data</h2>
        <p>DailyMate uses the collected data for various purposes:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>To provide and maintain the App</li>
            <li>To notify you about daily habit reminders and scheduled tasks (via Android AlarmManager)</li>
            <li>To allow you to participate in interactive features of our App when you choose to do so</li>
            <li>To provide customer support and analyze usage to improve user experience</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Security of Data</h2>
        <p>The security of your data is important to us. We implement industry-standard security measures including encrypted data transmission (HTTPS/SSL) and secure Firebase authentication protocols. However, remember that no method of transmission over the Internet or method of electronic storage is 100% secure.</p>

        <h2>5. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>Our App does not address anyone under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under 13.</p>

        <h2>6. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the effective date.</p>

